@model RecordsDeploymentStepViewModel
@*
    What an export of this module carries. The employees themselves; where they sit and what they
    lead belong to the dimension engine's step, which names them by the code exported here — so a
    plan carrying those without this one produces a file that cannot apply.

    Ordering is the one thing an operator can get wrong, so the form says it rather than leaving it
    to the ADR: lookup lists before anything that names a lookup value, employees before placements.
*@
<fieldset class="mb-3">
    <legend class="fs-6">@T["What to export"]</legend>

    <div class="form-check">
        <input asp-for="IncludeLookupLists" type="checkbox" class="form-check-input" value="true" />
        <label asp-for="IncludeLookupLists" class="form-check-label">@T["Lookup lists, with their entries"]</label>
        <div class="form-text">@T["The choices a form field offers, with each entry's code, both names, whether it is still offered and where it sits in the list. Apply this step before any step that names a lookup value."]</div>
    </div>

    <div class="form-check">
        <input asp-for="IncludeEmployees" type="checkbox" class="form-check-input" value="true" />
        <label asp-for="IncludeEmployees" class="form-check-label">@T["Employees, with their current employment status"]</label>
        <div class="form-text">@T["Everybody on record, including people who have left. An employee's earlier statuses are in the audit trail rather than on the record, so the status exported is the one they are in now."]</div>
    </div>
</fieldset>
